{:edb/db-before-t 1957 :edb/db-after-t 1958 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535270 50 #inst "2026-10-08T20:57:50.186Z" 13194139535270 true] [17592186068845 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340987 13194139535270 true] [17592186068846 1020 #edb/ref 17592186340980 13194139535270 true] [17592186069320 1017 #edb/ref 17592186067451 13194139535270 false] [17592186069320 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340991 13194139535270 true] [17592186069320 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535270 true] [17592186069320 1100 "$\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" 13194139535270 true] [17592186069320 1100 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int2x^{2}\\sin (2x)dx$?" 13194139535270 false] [17592186069320 1145 "We need to use integration by parts. \n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=2{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)}{2})(4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+2\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340980 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340981 13194139535270 true] [17592186340980 1089 "q-114946" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340980 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535270 true] [17592186340980 1100 "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.$" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340980 1113 #uuid "640a9063-5e5d-5f66-a705-18c7c5b67633" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340980 1145 "We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2} & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=25{x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 25{x}^{4}\\text{d}x=5{x}^{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}(5{x}^{5})-\\int (5{x}^{5})(\\frac{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe use integration by parts once again to evaluate $\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}={x}^{4} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})-\\int (\\frac{{x}^{5}}{5})(\\frac{1}{x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{1}{5}\\int {x}^{4}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10\\int {x}^{4}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-10(\\frac{{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{5}-\\frac{{x}^{5}}{25}+D) \\\\  & =5{x}^{5}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2{x}^{5}}{5}-10D \\\\  & ={x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})+C\\,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-10D.$ Finally then, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{e}25{x}^{4}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)^{2}\\text{d}x & ={[{x}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x+\\frac{2}{5})]}_{1}^{e} \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+\\frac{2}{5})]-[{1}^{5}(5{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)}^{2}-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+\\frac{2}{5})] \\\\  & =[{e}^{5}(5-2+\\frac{2}{5})]-\\frac{2}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340982 13194139535270 true] [17592186340981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340983 13194139535270 true] [17592186340981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340984 13194139535270 true] [17592186340981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340985 13194139535270 true] [17592186340981 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340986 13194139535270 true] [17592186340981 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535270 true] [17592186340981 1041 "selection" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340981 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340982 13194139535270 true] [17592186340981 1110 #uuid "ca7bfb65-4ff6-579f-8fa3-e6b2503ea858" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340982 1034 "\\frac{17{e}^{5}-2}{5}" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340982 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535270 true] [17592186340982 1111 #uuid "686d78c2-8c16-5b3b-928c-528e9bce2020" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340983 1034 "\\frac{4{e}^{5}+3}{5}" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340983 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535270 true] [17592186340983 1111 #uuid "99bcf369-caca-5778-8888-d4d039dceb38" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340984 1034 "{e}^{5}-1" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340984 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535270 true] [17592186340984 1111 #uuid "15dc5f51-f256-5559-818c-de91ad9b9ddf" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340985 1034 "\\frac{{e}^{5}-2}{5}" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340985 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535270 true] [17592186340985 1111 #uuid "6440635b-41f4-514c-a064-911b2c515b56" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340986 1034 "12{e}^{5}+2" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340986 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535270 true] [17592186340986 1111 #uuid "355864bc-5b6a-5489-bda2-cb7928ed1fa7" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340987 1017 #edb/ref 17592186340988 13194139535270 true] [17592186340987 1089 "q-352028" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340987 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139535270 true] [17592186340987 1100 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340987 1113 #uuid "2be1c0cd-adaf-53aa-b6b4-1aa499097229" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340987 1145 "We need to use integration by parts. We'll work out the indefinite integral first, and then proceed to work out the definite integral.\n\nIn this case, we define\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=27{x}^{2}\\, & ⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=54x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⟹\\,v=\\int \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(27{x}^{2})(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(54x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+18\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we use integration by parts to evaluate $\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.$ We take\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=1\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this case, the formula for integration by parts gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =x(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})\\cdot 1\\,dx \\\\  & =\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+18\\int x\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+18(\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9}+D) \\\\  & =-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=18D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}27{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={[-9{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+6x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =9{(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2}-2-2 \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}-4 \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340989 13194139535270 true] [17592186340988 1000 #edb/ref 17592186340990 13194139535270 true] [17592186340988 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139535270 true] [17592186340988 1041 "field-1" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340988 1104 #edb/ref 17592186340990 13194139535270 true] [17592186340988 1110 #uuid "70d19801-3829-53fc-8712-aa77403b3de1" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340989 1034 "\\pi^2+4" 13194139535270 true] [17592186340989 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 1